        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "04c009ee-c3d9-5583-9659-1e5ce316a78d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Carpentaria acuminata, Carpentaria, Panax, ginseng\n- Taxonomy: Araliaceae, genus, species\n- Places: Northern Territory, Australia, Gulf of Carpentaria, Port McArthur Tidal Wetlands System\n- Ecosystems: tidal wetlands\n\nFacts:\n- Carpentaria acuminata, also called the carpentaria palm, is the sole species in the genus Carpentaria.\n- Carpentaria acuminata is native to tropical coastal regions in the north of the Northern Territory, Australia.\n- Panax, also known as ginseng, belongs to the Araliaceae family.\n- The Port McArthur Tidal Wetlands System comprises a 994 km tract of tidal wetlands on the south-west coast of the Gulf of Carpentaria in the Northern Territory of Australia.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
